# Setting Bible — Characters

## Goal
Write the novel's canonical character roster from the outline.

## Requirements
{{#if skills}}
- The Skill Documents at the top are the grounding truth of this roster: follow them as authoritative instructions, not as background reading.
{{/if}}
- Output a list of plain strings; one character per item, self-contained.
- Cover the protagonist and every named character the outline anchors.
- For each character include: name, role (protagonist / supporting / antagonist), appearance, personality, desire, fear, speech style, and golden finger (rules, limits, side effects) when present.
- Skeleton-first: do not invent characters or details the outline does not anchor; the roster grows with the story.
- Keep the roster compact — about 300-500 words total.
- Timeless facts only: current ranks, relationship progress, or arc-stage states do not belong here.

Respond entirely in "{{ language }}".
